userStories.description:
**Goal** — Extend the pipeline event union, reporter contract, CallContext, and configuration with the typed phase-telemetry foundation.

**Motivation** — `IReporter` exposes exactly three hooks — `onRunStart`, `onStoryComplete`, `onRunEnd`; everything inside a story is invisible to reporters.

**Approach** — Telemetry is emitted from the **pipeline event bus**, not from the runtime dispatch-event channel (`src/runtime/dispatch-events.ts`), because reporters are wired to the pipeline bus by existing convention (`wireReporters`).

**Scope** — In: additive event and extension types plus validated reporter defaults. Out: event emitters, reporter fan-out, and exporter behavior belong to US-002 through US-008.

**Interface** — verbatim from the design:
```ts
export interface StoryPhaseCompletedEvent {
  type: "story:phase:completed";
  storyId: string;
  phase: string;                 // op name — same vocabulary as story:step
  outcome: "passed" | "failed" | "skipped" | "error";
  durationMs: number;
  costUsd: number;
  tier?: string;
  testStrategy?: TestStrategy;
  sessionModel?: "single-session" | "three-session";
  details?: PhaseDetails;
}
```
```ts
readonly phaseTelemetry?: {
  readonly testStrategy: TestStrategy;
  readonly sessionModel: "single-session" | "three-session";
  readonly tier: string;
};
```
```ts
interface PhaseEventBase { runId: string; scope: "story" | "run"; phase: string; storyId?: string; }
interface PhaseStartEvent extends PhaseEventBase { startTime: string }
interface PhaseCompleteEvent extends PhaseEventBase { outcome: "passed" | "failed" | "skipped" | "error"; durationMs: number; costUsd: number; tier?: string; testStrategy?: TestStrategy; sessionModel?: "single-session" | "three-session"; details?: PhaseDetails | RunPhaseDetails; }
```
Both hooks optional; existing reporters are unaffected.
